/-!
# Global sections avoiding a finite set of points

A global section `s` of a sheaf of `𝒪ₓ`-modules `F` *vanishes* at a point `x` of `X` when its
germ at `x` lies in `𝔪ₓ Fₓ`, that is, when its image in the fibre `Fₓ / 𝔪ₓ Fₓ` is zero. This
file proves that on a scheme over an **infinite** field a *single* global section can be chosen
which vanishes at none of a prescribed **finite** set of points, provided that at each of those
points some global section does not vanish.

The mechanism is the classical one. Vanishing at a fixed point `x` is a linear condition: the
global sections vanishing at `x` form a `Γ(X, 𝒪ₓ)`-submodule of `Γ(X, F)`, hence a `k`-subspace
for a scheme over `k`, and it is a *proper* subspace exactly when some global section does not
vanish at `x`. A vector space over an infinite field is not the union of finitely many proper
subspaces (`Subspace.top_mem_of_biUnion_eq_univ`), so a section outside all of them exists.

That some global section does not vanish at `x` is, by Nakayama's lemma, implied by the germs
at `x` of the global sections spanning the stalk `Fₓ` — being generated by global sections *at
the point* `x` — as soon as `Fₓ` is a non-zero finite `𝒪_{X, x}`-module.

The application is to the associated points of a coherent sheaf: on a quasi-compact locally
Noetherian scheme these are finite in number
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.finite_associatedPoints`), so a line bundle generated by its
global sections has a global section vanishing at none of them. This is the genericity half of
`lem:deg-general-hyperplane` of the blueprint chapter on the degree of the isogeny, stated
without reference to a projective embedding: the blueprint chooses a hyperplane
`∑ⱼ aⱼ Tⱼ` avoiding finitely many points of `𝐏ᴺ` by exactly this argument, and the linear forms
`∑ⱼ aⱼ Tⱼ` are nothing but the global sections of `𝒪(1)|_X`.

## Main definitions

- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.VanishesAt`: a global section vanishes at a point.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.vanishingSubmodule`: the global sections vanishing at a
  point, as a `Γ(X, 𝒪ₓ)`-submodule of `Γ(X, F)`.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.IsGloballyGeneratedAt`: the germs at a point of the global
  sections span the stalk there.

## Main results

- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_not_vanishesAt`: **Nakayama's lemma in the form of a
  non-vanishing section** — if `F` is generated by its global sections at `x` and `Fₓ` is a
  non-zero finite `𝒪_{X, x}`-module, some global section of `F` does not vanish at `x`.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_forall_not_vanishesAt`: **a global section avoiding
  finitely many points**, over an infinite field.
- `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_forall_associatedPoints_not_vanishesAt`: a global
  section vanishing at no associated point of a coherent sheaf.

## Implementation notes

The `k`-vector space structure on `Γ(X, F)` for a scheme `X` over `Spec k` is not an instance:
it is built inside the proof of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_forall_not_vanishesAt` by restricting the
`Γ(X, 𝒪ₓ)`-module structure along `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.overRingHom`, and it is invisible
in every statement.

## Blueprint

This file contributes the genericity step of `lem:deg-general-hyperplane` of
`curve_estimates/28_degree_of_the_isogeny.tex`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits Opposite SheafOfModules TopologicalSpace

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-- A global section `s` of a sheaf of modules `F` **vanishes at** a point `x` of `X` if its
germ at `x` lies in `𝔪ₓ Fₓ`, equivalently if its image in the fibre `Fₓ / 𝔪ₓ Fₓ` is zero. -/
def VanishesAt (F : X.Modules) (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (x : X) : Prop :=
  germₗ F (⟨x, trivial⟩ : (⊤ : X.Opens)) s ∈
    IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) •
      (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x))

/-- The global sections vanishing at a point `x` form a `Γ(X, 𝒪ₓ)`-submodule of `Γ(X, F)`. -/
noncomputable def vanishingSubmodule (F : X.Modules) (x : (⊤ : X.Opens)) :
    Submodule Γ(X, ⊤) Γ(F, ⊤) :=
  Submodule.comap (germₗ F x)
    (Submodule.restrictScalars Γ(X, ⊤)
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x.1) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x.1) (F.presheaf.stalk x.1))))

lemma mem_vanishingSubmodule_iff (F : X.Modules) (s : Γ(F, ⊤)) (x : X) :
    s ∈ F.vanishingSubmodule ⟨x, trivial⟩ ↔ F.VanishesAt s x := Iff.rfl

/-- A sheaf of modules is **generated by its global sections at a point** `x` if the germs at
`x` of its global sections span the stalk `Fₓ` over the local ring `𝒪_{X, x}`. -/
def IsGloballyGeneratedAt (F : X.Modules) (x : X) : Prop :=
  Submodule.span (X.presheaf.stalk x)
    (Set.range (germₗ F (⟨x, trivial⟩ : (⊤ : X.Opens)))) = ⊤

/-- **A vector space over an infinite field is not the union of finitely many proper
subspaces**, in the form used below: if each of finitely many subspaces misses some vector,
then a single vector misses all of them. -/
private theorem exists_forall_notMem {k M ι : Type*} [Field k] [Infinite k] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module k M] {Z : Set ι} (hZ : Z.Finite) (W : ι → Submodule k M)
    (hW : ∀ i ∈ Z, ∃ m : M, m ∉ W i) : ∃ m : M, ∀ i ∈ Z, m ∉ W i := by
  by_contra h
  push Not at h
  have hcov : ⋃ p ∈ hZ.toFinset.image W, (p : Set M) = Set.univ := by
    refine Set.eq_univ_of_forall fun m ↦ ?_
    obtain ⟨i, hi, hm⟩ := h m
    exact Set.mem_biUnion (Finset.mem_image_of_mem W (hZ.mem_toFinset.2 hi)) hm
  obtain ⟨i, hi, hiW⟩ := Finset.mem_image.1 (Subspace.top_mem_of_biUnion_eq_univ hcov)
  obtain ⟨m, hm⟩ := hW i (hZ.mem_toFinset.1 hi)
  exact hm (hiW ▸ Submodule.mem_top)

/-- **Nakayama's lemma in the form of a non-vanishing global section.** If `F` is generated by
its global sections at `x` and the stalk `Fₓ` is a non-zero finite module over the local ring
`𝒪_{X, x}`, then some global section of `F` does not vanish at `x`.

Indeed, were every global section to vanish at `x`, the germs would all lie in `𝔪ₓ Fₓ`; since
they span, `Fₓ = 𝔪ₓ Fₓ`, which Nakayama's lemma forbids for a non-zero finite module over a
local ring. -/
theorem exists_not_vanishesAt (F : X.Modules) (x : X) (hx : Nontrivial (F.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hfin : Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hgg : F.IsGloballyGeneratedAt x) :
    ∃ s : Γ(F, ⊤), ¬ F.VanishesAt s x := by
  have : Nontrivial (F.presheaf.stalk x) := hx
  have : Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x) := hfin
  by_contra h
  push Not at h
  have hsub : Set.range (germₗ F (⟨x, trivial⟩ : (⊤ : X.Opens))) ≤
      (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) •
        (⊤ : Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x)) :
          Submodule (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x)) := by
    rintro - ⟨s, rfl⟩
    exact h s
  have hann : Module.annihilator (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x) ≠ ⊤ := fun hc ↦
    (not_subsingleton _) (Module.annihilator_eq_top_iff.1 hc)
  have hjac : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (X.presheaf.stalk x) ≤
      (Module.annihilator (X.presheaf.stalk x) (F.presheaf.stalk x)).jacobson :=
    (IsLocalRing.jacobson_eq_maximalIdeal _ hann).ge
  have hle := Submodule.span_le.2 hsub
  rw [hgg] at hle
  exact Submodule.top_ne_ideal_smul_of_le_jacobson_annihilator hjac (le_antisymm hle le_top)

variable (k : Type u) [Field k] [Infinite k]

/-- **A global section avoiding finitely many prescribed points.** Let `X` be a scheme over an
infinite field `k` and let `F` be a sheaf of `𝒪ₓ`-modules. If `Z` is a finite set of points of
`X` at each of which *some* global section of `F` does not vanish, then a *single* global
section of `F` vanishes at no point of `Z`.

The global sections vanishing at a point form a `k`-subspace of `Γ(X, F)`, proper by
hypothesis, and a vector space over an infinite field is not the union of finitely many proper
subspaces. -/
theorem exists_forall_not_vanishesAt [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (F : X.Modules) {Z : Set X}
    (hZ : Z.Finite) (hF : ∀ x ∈ Z, ∃ s : Γ(F, ⊤), ¬ F.VanishesAt s x) :
    ∃ s : Γ(F, ⊤), ∀ x ∈ Z, ¬ F.VanishesAt s x := by
  let _ : Module k Γ(X, ⊤) := Module.compHom _ (Scheme.overRingHom k X)
  let _ : Module k Γ(F, ⊤) := Module.compHom _ (Scheme.overRingHom k X)
  have : IsScalarTower k Γ(X, ⊤) Γ(F, ⊤) := ⟨fun c r s ↦ mul_smul _ r s⟩
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := exists_forall_notMem (k := k) hZ
    (fun x ↦ Submodule.restrictScalars k (F.vanishingSubmodule ⟨x, trivial⟩))
    fun x hx ↦ hF x hx
  exact ⟨s, hs⟩

/-- **A global section vanishing at no associated point of a coherent sheaf.** On a quasi-compact
locally Noetherian scheme `X` over an infinite field, a sheaf of modules `L` generated by its
global sections at each associated point of a quasi-coherent sheaf `F`, and with non-zero
finite stalks there, has a global section vanishing at none of them.

This is the genericity half of `lem:deg-general-hyperplane`: the associated points of `F` are
finite in number by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.finite_associatedPoints`, and the
blueprint's hyperplane avoiding them is such a global section of `L = 𝒪(1)|_X`.

As in `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.finite_associatedPoints`, the coherence of `F` enters
through the hypothesis `hF` that its sections over each affine open form a finite module. -/
theorem exists_forall_associatedPoints_not_vanishesAt [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] [CompactSpace X]
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (hF : ∀ V : X.affineOpens, Module.Finite Γ(X, V.1) Γ(F, V.1)) (L : X.Modules)
    (hne : ∀ x ∈ F.associatedPoints, Nontrivial (L.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hfin : ∀ x ∈ F.associatedPoints,
      Module.Finite (X.presheaf.stalk x) (L.presheaf.stalk x))
    (hgg : ∀ x ∈ F.associatedPoints, L.IsGloballyGeneratedAt x) :
    ∃ s : Γ(L, ⊤), ∀ x ∈ F.associatedPoints, ¬ L.VanishesAt s x :=
  exists_forall_not_vanishesAt k L (finite_associatedPoints F hF) fun x hx ↦
    exists_not_vanishesAt L x (hne x hx) (hfin x hx) (hgg x hx)

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
